                  %th
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝕊
                            %mi Sym
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Sym}
                  %th
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝕊
                            %mi Seq
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Seq}
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+object"} commutative monoid object
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} no
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} yes
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} no
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} no
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} no
            %p
              Explicitly, by the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Day+convolution#Monoids"} Day convolutions – Properties – Monoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
              on the site, and as such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Orth
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Orth}
              is the one given by the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊕
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{V_1} \wedge S^{V_2} \longrightarrow S^{V_1 \oplus V_2}
            %p
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Sym
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Sym}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Seq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Seq}
              the ones given by the canonical natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n_1} \wedge S^{n_2} \longrightarrow S^{n_1 + n_2}
                    \\,.
          %p
            Therefore we may consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
            over the restrictions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            from def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardRepresentativeOfTheSphereSpectrum"}
          #HighlyStructuredSpectraAsDayConvolutionSModules.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The category of right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi Orth
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Orth}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Sym
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Sym}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Seq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Seq}
              from def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardRepresentativeOfTheSphereSpectrum"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
              by prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropertiesOfTopologicalDiagramCategoriesForSpectra"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RestrictionsOfSphereSpectrumAreStillMonoidObjects"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
              (in
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Orth
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi r
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi OrthSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{Orth} Mod_r \simeq OrthSpec(Top)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Sym
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi r
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SymSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{Sym} Mod_r \simeq SymSpec(Top)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Seq
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi r
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{Seq} Mod_r \simeq SeqSpec(Top)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}
              for any of the three monoids. By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Day+convolution#Monoids"} Day convolutions – Properties – Monoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              are equivalently right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules+over+monoidal+functors"} modules over monoidal functors
              over the monoidal functor corresponding to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}
              as in remark
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RestrictionsOfSphereSpectrumAreStillMonoidObjects"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Sym
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Sym}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Seq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Seq}
              they are functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi sSet
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon Sym \longrightarrow sSet^{\ast/}
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Seq
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msup
                        %mi sSet
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon Seq \longrightarrow sSet^{\ast/}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi q
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_p \wedge S^{q}  \longrightarrow X_{p+q}
            %p
              satisfying the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              property. In the present case this action property says that these morphisms are determined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_p \wedge S^1 \longrightarrow X_{p+1}
            %p
              under the isomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi p
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∧
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^p \simeq S^1 \wedge S^{p-1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym
              is the equivariance under the symmetric group actions in the definition of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            %p
              Similarly, modules over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Orth
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Orth}
              are equivalently functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi V
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi W
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_V \wedge S^{W}  \longrightarrow X_{V \oplus W}
            %p
              etc. and their functoriality embodies the
              = succeed "-equivariance" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
          #PreExcisiveFunctorsAreSModules.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              For completeness, we may, trivially, add to the three statements in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HighlyStructuredSpectraAsDayConvolutionSModules"}
              the equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi r
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S} Mod_r \simeq [Top^{\ast/}_{fin}, Top^{\ast/}]
                    \\,,
            %p
              which holds tautologically because by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardRepresentativeOfTheSphereSpectrum"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
              is in fact the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi fin
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi Top
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Day
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([Top^{\ast/}_{fin}, Top^{\ast/}],\otimes_{Day})
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            %p
              Now the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+excisive+functors"} model structure on excisive functors
              shows that the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Top^{\ast/}_{fin}, Top^{\ast/}]
              constitutes a model for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %p
              Hence we may read prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HighlyStructuredSpectraAsDayConvolutionSModules"}
              as saying that while restricting the domain of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excisive+functors"} excisive functors
              breaks their property of being a model for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              structure first of all becomes non-tautological after restriction and second restores the property of the objects to model spectra.
          #SymmetricSmashProductOfDiagramSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              By remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RestrictionsOfSphereSpectrumAreStillMonoidObjects"}
              the categories
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi Sym
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Sym} Mod_r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Orth
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Orth} Mod_r
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Orth
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Orth} Mod_r
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+object"} commutative monoid object
              and as such they inherit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              structure
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ∧
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mi dia
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod, \wedge_{\mathbb{S}_{dia}})
            %p
              Via prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HighlyStructuredSpectraAsDayConvolutionSModules"}
              this is equivalently symmetric monoidal product structure
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SymSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (SymSpec(Top), \wedge)
            %p
              on the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi OrthSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (OrthSpec(Top), \wedge)
            %p
              on that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
          #SystemOfStructuredSpectraAndDiagrams.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Combined with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-forgetful+adjunctions"} free-forgetful adjunctions
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊣
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dashv
              underlying objects) the situation described by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropertiesOfTopologicalDiagramCategoriesForSpectra"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HighlyStructuredSpectraAsDayConvolutionSModules"}
              jointly is the following diagram of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
