          %p
            In order to conveniently speak about all columns of the system of adjunctions in remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SystemOfStructuredSpectraAndDiagrams"}
            in a unified way, we introduce the following notation.
          #NotationForGenericDiagramSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dia
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Orth
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Sym
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Seq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dia \in \{Top^{\ast/, Orth, Sym, Seq}\}
              generically for any one of the four sites in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalDiagramCategoriesForSpectra"}
            %p
              Accordingly we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Orth
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Sym
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Seq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} \in \{\mathbb{S}, \mathbb{S}_{Orth}, \mathbb{S}_{Sym}, \mathbb{S}_{Seq}\}
              generically for any one of the four incarnations of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              according to def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardRepresentativeOfTheSphereSpectrum"}
            %p Finally we will write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi seq
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
