            %p
              of lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SModulesAsEnrichedFunctors"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+enriched+functors"} model structure on enriched functors
              (
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"}> Piacenza 91
              ) see hereodel structure on topological spaces#ModelStructureOnTopEnrichedFunctors).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, def. 6.1
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              To see that indeed all the adjunctions here are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunctions"} Quillen adjunctions
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropertiesOfTopologicalDiagramCategoriesForSpectra"}
              and lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SModulesAsEnrichedFunctors"}
              all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints"} right adjoints
              are given by restrictions of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
          #TheStrictModelStructuresOnDiagramSpectra.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p The model structure
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi seq
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi strict
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{seq} Mod_{strict}
                    \\simeq
                    SeqSpec(Top)_{strict}
            %p
              in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra#TheStrictModelStructure"} strict model structure on topological sequential spectra
          %p
            The strict model structures of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of the given diagrams of homotopy types, hence a homotopy theory of pre-spectra. To obtain from this the genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            of genuine spectra we need to restrict this to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
          #StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For any of the four categories of spectra in prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SystemOfAdjunctionsForDiagramSpectra"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NotationForGenericDiagramSpectra"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is an
                  %em Omega-spectrum
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi seq
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq^\ast X
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega+spectrum"} Omega spectrum
                  in the standard sense of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %em stable weak homotopy equivalence
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi seq
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} seq^\ast(f)
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} stable weak homotopy equivalence
                  in the standard sense of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
                  (an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  on all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
                  of sequential spectra);
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %em stable equivalence
                  if for all Omega-spectra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  in the above sense, the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi E
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi strict
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f,E]_{strict}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi E
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi strict
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,E]_{strict}
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
                  of the strict model structure of prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS00, def. 8.3 with the notation from p. 21
            )
          %p
            The following proposition says that def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
            makes sense, in that if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
            of the strict model structures at the stable equivalences exists (which we check
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "ProofOfTheStableModelStructure"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
          #StableEquivalencesBetweenOmegaSpectraAreStrictWeakEquivalences.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The weak equivalences in the strict model structure (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
              are related as follows:
            %ol
              %li
                %p Every weak equivalence with respect to the strict model structure is a stable equivalence.
              %li
                %p
                  Every stable equivalence between Omega-spectra (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, lemma 8.11
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              The first statement follows by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
              since weak equivalences become isomorphisms in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            %p
              For the second statement, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              be a stable equivalence between Omega-spectra. Then by definition, in particular
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi strict
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi strict
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [f,X]_{strict} \;\colon\; [Y,X]_{strict} \longrightarrow [X,X]_{strict}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [id_X] \in [X,X]_{strict}
              is an inverse to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              of the strict model structure. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              represents an isomorphism in the strict homotopy category and is hence a weak equivalence in the strict model structure.
          %h3#FreeSpectra Free spectra
          %blockquote
            %p
              This is a technical section with discussion of certain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              objects in the categories of spectra of prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HighlyStructuredSpectraAsDayConvolutionSModules"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#ProofOfTheStableModelStructure"} below
              %a{:href => "#QuillenEquivalencesOfStableModelStructures"} further below
              and
              %a{:href => "#MonoidalStableModelStructure"} then
              the proof that the model structure is monoidal.
          %p
            The concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+spectrum"} free spectrum
            is a generalization of that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+types"} stable homotopy types
            of free spectra are precisely those of iterated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+objects"} loop space objects
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+spectra"} model structures on spectra
            analogous to the role of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            below).
          %p
            Moreover, while free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
            are just re-indexed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            and free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            in addition come with suitably freely generated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjunctsOfFreeSpectrumInclusionsAreOrAreNotStableWeakHomotopyEquivalences"}
            below) where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjuncts"} adjuncts
            of certain canonical inclusions of free spectra are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+weak+homotopy+equivalences"} stable weak homotopy equivalences
            for sequential and orthogonal spectra, but
            %em not
            for symmetric spectra. The fine analysis of this phenomenon is crucial in the proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            between the stable model structures on the four models of spectra (theorem
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenEquivalencesBetweenStableModelStructuresOnDiagramSpectra"}
          #FreeStructuredSpectrum.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dia
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi fin
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Orth
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Seq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dia \in \{Top^{\ast/}_{fin}, Orth, Sym, Seq\}
              and for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi seq
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Seq
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)_n
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod \stackrel{seq^\ast}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{S}_{Seq}Mod \simeq SeqSpec(Top) \stackrel{(-)_n}{\longrightarrow} Top^{\ast/}
            %p
              that sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+spectrum"} structured spectrum
              (notation as in def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NotationForGenericDiagramSpectra"}
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi dia
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F^{dia}_n \;\colon\; Top^{\ast/} \longrightarrow \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is called the
              = succeed "-functor." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+structured+spectrum"} free structured spectrum
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+units"} adjunction units
              in the sequence of adjunctions equip these with canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi Seq
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                          %mi Seq
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi Sym
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                          %mi Sym
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi Orth
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                          %mi Orth
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Top
                          %mi fin
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_n^{Seq}
                    \\stackrel{f_n^{Seq}}{\longrightarrow}
                    F_n^{Sym}
                    \\stackrel{f_n^{Sym}}{\longrightarrow}
                    F_n^{Orth}
                    \\stackrel{f_n^{Orth}}{\longrightarrow}
                    F_n^{Top^{\ast/}_{fin}}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, section 8
            )
          #ExplicitExpressionForFreeSpectra.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              Under the equivalence of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SModulesAsEnrichedFunctors"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+spectrum"} free spectrum
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
