              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(q-k)
              equivalently become quotients of just the left action. Formally this is due to the existence of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi O
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo +
                            %mo ∧
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mi O
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi q
