          %h2#PartII Part II. Model categories of diagram spectra
          %p
            We now discuss equipping the diagram categories of
            %a{:href => "#PartI"} part I
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures, each presenting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (infinity,1)-category of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            between these categories becomes a system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            between these model structures.
          %h3#ModelStructuresForPlainSpectra 5.-10.) Model structures on plain spectra
          %p
            Here we discuss model structures for plain spectra,
            %a{:href => "ModelStructuresOnRingSpectraAndModuleSpectra"} below
            we discuss model structures for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
          %h4#ProofOfTheStableModelStructure The stable model structures
          #StableModelStructuresOnDiagramSpectra.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              of the strict model structures of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              at the stable equivalences of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
              exists, to be called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em stable model structures
            %p
              Explicitly, there is a model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod_{stable}
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  cofibrations are those of the strict model structure (prop.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %li
                %p
                  weak equivalences are the stable equivalences (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
            %p
              and the identity functors constitute a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi stable
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi id
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi id
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi strict
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod_{stable}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{id}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{id}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod_{strict}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod_{stable}
              is a
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+model+category"}> compactly generated model category
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"}> proper model category
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Top
                          %mi Quillen
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{Quillen}
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"}> enriched model category
                  \.
            %p Specifically, this specializes to
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  fro
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dia
                          %mo =
                          %mi Seq
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia = Seq
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dia
                          %mo =
                          %mi Sym
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia = Sym
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dia
                          %mo =
                          %mi Orth
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia = Orth
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Dia
                          %mo =
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Top
                            %mi CW
                            %mrow
                              %mo *
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia = Top^{\ast/}_{CW}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+excisive+functors"} model structure for excisive functors
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS00, theorem 9.2
            )
          %p
            We give the proof of theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableModelStructuresOnDiagramSpectra"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#StableModelStructureOnDiagramSpectraProof"} below
          %p
            The generating cofibrations and acylic cofibrations are going to be the those induced via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
            of representables from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            (giving the strict model structure), together with an additional set of morphisms to the generating acylic cofibrations that will force fibrant objects to be Omega-spectra. To that end we need the following little preliminary.
          #CorepresentingForAdjunctOfStructureMapsAreStableEquivalences.num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              By construction, the morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_n
              of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingOfAdjunctsOfStructureMapsExists"}
              are stable equivalences according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
          %p We need to in addition resolve them by suitable cofibrations:
          #ResolutionOfCorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                    %mi Cyl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi def
                        %mo .
                        %mi retr
                        %mo .
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda_n
                    \\colon
                    F_{n+} \stackrel{k_n}{\longrightarrow}
                    Cyl(\lambda_n)
                    \\stackrel{def.retr.}{\longrightarrow}
                    F_n S^0
            %p
              be a factorization of the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_n
              of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingOfAdjunctsOfStructureMapsExists"}
              and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps"}
              through a strict cofibration followed by a strict weak equivalence (e.g. through its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinder"} mapping cylinder
              followed by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retraction"} deformation retraction
              (see
              = succeed "))." do
                %a{:href => "mapping+cylinder#FactorizationOfMapThroughMappingCylinderFollowedByDeformationRetraction"} here
          %p With this we may state the classes of morphisms that are going to be shown to be the classes of generating (acyclic) cofibrations for the stable model structures:
          #GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p Recall the sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I \coloneqq \{S^{n-1} \hookrightarrow D^n\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J \coloneqq \{D^n \hookrightarrow D^n \times I\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
            %p
              of generating cofibrations and generating acyclic cofibrations, respectively, of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝕊
                              %mi Dia
                            %mi FreeMod
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F I \coloneqq \{ y(x) \otimes i_+ \}_{{x \in \mathbb{S}_{Dia} FreeMod} \atop {i \in I}}
            %p
              for the class of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+spectra"} free spectra
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeStructuredSpectrum"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              above, which by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitExpressionForFreeSpectra"}
              is equivalently the set of morphisms arising as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              with a topological generating cofibration of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi FreeMod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} FreeMod
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
              from lemma
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SModulesAsEnrichedFunctors"}
            %p Similarly, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝕊
                              %mi Dia
                            %mi FreeMod
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F J \coloneqq \{ y(x) \otimes j_+ \}_{{x \in \mathbb{S}_{Dia}FreeMod} \atop {j \in J}}
                    \\,,
            %p
              for the set of morphisms arising as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              with a generating acyclic cofibration of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              (with basepoint adjoined).
            %p Finally write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K
                    \\coloneqq
                    F J
                    \\;\sqcup\;
                    \\{
                    k_n \Box i_+
                    \\}_{{n \in \mathbb{N}} \atop {i \in I}}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F J
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+products"} pushout products
              of the resolved maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ResolutionOfCorepresentationOfAdjunctsOfStructureMaps"}
              with the elements in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, def. 9.3
            )
          #CofibrantGenerationOfStrictModelStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              The sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F I
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F J
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
              (disregarding the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              there) are, respectively sets of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+cofibrations"} generating cofibrations
              and generating acyclic cofibrations for the strict model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Dia}Mod_{strict}
              (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_12 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              the strict model structure is equivalently the projective pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+enriched+functors"} model structure on topologically enriched functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi strict
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi Dia
                    %msup
                      %mi FreeMod
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}_{Dia}Mod_{strict} \simeq [\mathbb{S}_{Dia}FreeMod^{op}, Top^{\ast/}]_{proj}
                    \\,.
            %p
              With this the statement follows by the proof of
              %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces#ProjectiveModelStructureOnTopEnrichedFunctors"} this
              theorem.
          #ElementsOfKAreStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_9 Lemma
            %p
              Every element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a cofibration with respect to the strict model structure (prop.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %li
                %p
                  a stable equivalence (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_13 Proof
            %p
              First regarding strict cofibrations: By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F J
              have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against the strict fibrations, hence in particular they are strict cofibrations. Moreover, by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal-Tierney+calculus"} Joyal-Tierney calculus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              has left lifting against any acyclic strict fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              has left lifting against
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod_{strict}
              behaving like a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              for one argument a relative CW-complex, the latter is still a strict acyclic fibration. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              by construction is a strict cofibration, the lifting follows and hence also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              is a strict cofibration.
            %p
              Regarding stable equivalences: The morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F J
              by design are strict weak equivalences, hence they are in particular stable equivalences. Similarly, the morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n
              by construction, by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              and by remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingForAdjunctOfStructureMapsAreStableEquivalences"}
              are stable equivalences. Hence the derived hom (…expand…) out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              is the homotopy pullback of a weak equivalence, hence is a weak equivalence, hence on the homotopy category an iso.
          %p
            The point of the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            is to make the following true:
          #KInjectivesAreAcyclicCofibrations.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_10 Lemma
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia} Mod
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphism"} injective morphism
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              from def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p it is a fibration in the strict model structure (hence degreewise a fibration)
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+squares"} commuting squares
                  of structure map compatibility on the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectra"} sequential spectra
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mover
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mtd
                                %mi Ω
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mi n
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mover
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mtd
                                %mi Ω
                                %msub
                                  %mi Y
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        X_n  &amp;\overset{\tilde\sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega X_{n+1}
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        Y_n &amp;\underset{\tilde \sigma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega Y_{n+1}
                        }
                %p
                  exhibit
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, prop. 9.5
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_14 Proof
            %p
              By prop
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantGenerationOfStrictModelStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F J
              alone characterizes strict fibrations, hence degreewise fibrations. Lifting against the remaining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
              morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo □
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_n \Box i_+
              is, by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal-Tierney+calculus"} Joyal-Tierney calculus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_+
              against the dual pullback product of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{k_n}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{k_n}
              is a weak homotopy equivalence. But by construction (lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingOfAdjunctsOfStructureMapsExists"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{k_n}
              is the comparison morphism into the homotopy pullback under consideration.
          #KInjectivesObjectsAreOmegaSpectra.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              from def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
          #KInjectiveStableEquivalencesAreStrictEquivalences.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_11 Lemma
            %p
              A morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
              which is both
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a stable equivalence (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
                  (with respect to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  from def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForDiagramSpectra"}
            %p
              is an acyclic fibration in the strict model structure of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              of topological spaces;
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, corollary 9.8
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_15 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to B
              be both a stable equivalence as well as a
              = succeed "-injective" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              contains, by prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantGenerationOfStrictModelStructure"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is in particular a strict fibration, hence a degreewise fibration. Therefore the fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              in the strict model structure.
            %blockquote
              %p We now want to claim that:
            %p
              It follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \ast
              is a stable equivalence.
            %blockquote
              %p#WhyFIsStablyEquivalentToThePoint This needs some explanation:
              %p
                Consider for any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi dia
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
                the cofiber sequence
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi hocof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi Σ
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B,E]_{strict} \overset{p^\ast}{\longrightarrow} [X,E]_{strict} \overset{}{\longrightarrow} [hocof(p),E]_{strict} \longrightarrow [\Sigma B, E]_{strict} \overset{\Sigma p^\ast}{\longrightarrow}[\Sigma X,E]_{strict}
              %p
                This kind of sequence is long exact for every pointed model category, not necessarily stable. Then let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                be any Omega-spectrum. By assumption it follows then that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^\ast
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma p^\ast
                are isomorphisms, so that exactness implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi hocof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [hocof(p),E]_{strict} = 0
                for all Omega-spectra
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %p
                Now use that on underlying sequential spectra there is a stable weak homotopy equivalence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hocof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi hofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hocof(p) \longrightarrow \Sigma hofib(p) = \Sigma F
                (
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1#HomotopyCofiberSequencesAreHomotopyFiberSequencesInSpectra"}> prop.
                ). Since suspension is preserved by passing to underlying sequential spectra, and since stable homotopy groups by definition are those of the underlying sequential spectra, and since stable weak equivalences are in particular stable equivalences (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableWeakHomotopyEquivalenceIsStableEquivalence"}
                below) it follows that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma F, E]_{strict}
                for all Omega-spectra
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi E
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi strict
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [F, \Omega E]_{strict} = 0
                for all Omega-spectra.
              %p
                We are to conclude that hence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \ast
                is a stable equivalence. But to conclude this we now need to know that every Omega-spectrum in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi dia
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod
                is in the image under
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                of an Omega-spectrum, up to strict equivalence. Indeed one shows that there is a shift functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sh
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sh
                on structured spectra and that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi sh
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{}{\longrightarrow} \Omega sh E
                is degreewise a weak homotopy equivalence.
            %p
              Observe also that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "-injective" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "injective+or+projective+morphism#ClosureProperties"} closure properties
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective object
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectivesObjectsAreOmegaSpectra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is an Omega-spectrum. Together this implies with prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableEquivalencesBetweenOmegaSpectraAreStrictWeakEquivalences"}
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \ast
              is a weak equivalence in the strict model structure, hence degreewise a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{\bullet \geq 1}(f_n)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and for each homotopy group in positive degree.
            %p
              To infer from this the remaining case that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f_0)
              is an isomorphism, observe that, by assumption of
              = succeed "-injectivity," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectivesAreAcyclicCofibrations"}
              gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n
              is a homotopy pullback (in topological spaces) of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega (f_{n+1})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
