              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectiveStableEquivalencesAreStrictEquivalences"}
              it is a strict acylic fibration.
          #StableModelStructureOnDiagramSpectraProof.proof
            %h6#proof_18 Proof
            %p
              (of theorem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableModelStructuresOnDiagramSpectra"}
            %p
              The non-trivial points to check are the two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi stable
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi weq
                      %mi stable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi fib
                      %mi stable
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cof_{stable}\cap weq_{stable} \;,\; fib_{stable})
              is a weak factorization system follows from lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfRelativeKCellComplexesAreTheStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations"}
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableAcyclicFibrationsAreEquivalentlyStrictAcyclicFibrations"}
              the stable acyclic fibrations are equivalently the strict acyclic fibrations and hence the weak factorization system
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi stable
