          .proof
            %h6#proof_21 Proof
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RetractsOfRelativeKCellComplexesAreTheStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrations"}
              the stable fibrations are equivalently the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+morphisms"} injective morphisms
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KInjectivesAreAcyclicCofibrations"}
              these are characterized by data that is preserved by right Quillen functors with respect to the strict model structure. Moreover by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableAcyclicFibrationsAreEquivalentlyStrictAcyclicFibrations"}
              the stable acyclic fibrations are equivalently the strict acyclic fibrations, which are of course also preserved by right Quillen functors for the strict model structure. Therefore the statement follows with prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnDiagramSpectra"}
          #ProofOfQuillenEquivalencesOfStableModelStructures.proof
            %h6#proof_idea_2 Proof idea
            %p
              (of theorem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenEquivalencesBetweenStableModelStructuresOnDiagramSpectra"}
            %p
              With lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjunctionsBetweenDiagramSpectraAreStableQuillenAdjunctions"}
              it is sufficient to show that all the total
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalences"} adjoint equivalences
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
              for Quillen equivalences, it is sufficient to show this for all the (composite) adjunctions whose right adjoint does
              %em not
              point to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi Sym
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{Sym}Mod
            %p
              In these cases, theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationBetweenStableEquivalencesAndStableWeakHomotopyEquivalencesForDiagramSpectra"}
              implies that the right adjoint functor preserves and reflects weak equivalence (a morphism in its domain is a stable equivalence precisely if its image is).
            %p
              In such a case, for checking a Quillen equivalence it is sufficient to check that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              is a weak equivalence on all cofibrant objects (…citation…).
            %p
              Since both adjoints in the present case preserve
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+lifting+property"} homotopy lifting property
            %p (…)
            %p (…)
          %h3#ModelStructuresOnRingSpectraAndModuleSpectra 11.-16.) Model structures on ring spectra and module spectra
          %h4#MonoidalStableModelStructure Monoidal model structure
          .num_theorem
