          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMSS00"}> MMSS 00, theorem 12.1 (iii) with prop. 12.3
            )
          %p We give the proof below (…) after a sequence of lemmas.
          #PushoutSmashProductOfStableCofibsIsStableCofib.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_16 Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout+product"} pushout product
              of two cofibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi dia
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_{dia}Mod_{stable}
              is again a cofibration.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_22 Proof
            %p
              A general abstract fact about
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-products"} pushout-products
              (
              %a{:href => "#HoveyShipleySmith00"}> Hovey-Shipley-Smith 00, prop. 5.3.4
              , see
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "pushout-product#PushoutProductOfCofClassIsCofClassOfPushoutProduct"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_1, I_2
              two classes of morphisms in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+colimits"} finite colimits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi i
                    %mi Cof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_i Cof
              for their saturated classes, then under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product"} pushout-product
              = succeed ":" do
