                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\gamma(X) \otimes^L \gamma(Y)) \otimes^L \gamma(Z)
                    \\to \gamma(X\otimes Y)\otimes^L \gamma(Z)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+axiom+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} monoid axiom
              (but not by the pushout-product axiom!), the horizontal maps in the square in the bottom right (labeled
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋆
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
              in the first place, and that under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              the total top zig-zag is equal to the image of that total bottom zig-zag. But by functoriality of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
