                    \\gamma(p_X \otimes p_Y \otimes p_Z)
                    \\circ
                    \\gamma(j_{Q X} \otimes j_{Q Y} \otimes j_{Q Z})^{-1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The same argument applies to left tensoring with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Q
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Q Z
              instead of right tensoring, and so in both cases we reduce to the same morphism in the homotopy category, thus showing the associativity condition on the transformation that exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
